}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''886-2''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==

886-2 is effectively a mashup of the most noteworthy aspects from [[Talents|Talented]] [[Cat God the Great (Special Cat)|Cat God the Golden]] and [[Filibuster Cat X (Special Cat)|Metafilibuster]], possessing a comedically long foreswing animation with an insanely powerful payout that strikes out the entire field. The effective reach on her [[Long Distance]] [[Multi-Hit]] pierces up to 1,000 range, or an additional 600 range from her standing range, which means she won't be whiffing her attacks all too often. The aim of the game is to protect 886-2 long enough for her to finish her attack animation; this means squeezing the most out of your meatshields to prevent frontline enemies from reaching her, abusing peons as stepping stones to give her a much safer vantage point to start attacking from, and pairing her up with certain [[Cat Cannon]]s like [[Ototo Corps#Breakerblast|Breakerblast]] or [[Ototo Corps#Thunderbolt|Thunderbolt]] to ward off impending danger at a moment's notice. She simply doesn't have the means to protect herself otherwise, since her first Multi-Hit deals negligible damage and provides no crowd-controlling effects whatsoever. Furthermore, while 886-2 is not frail, a majority of her survivability comes from her range in combination with [[Dodge Attack]], so there's a massive RNG factor to using her against targets who outrange her like [[Wicked Face]], [[Othom]], and [[Ackey]]. You are highly encouraged to plan a consistent means to land her second Multi-Hit frequently rather than relying exclusively on hopes and prayers to get the job done. This is where her [[Conjure]] finds its best usage, besides Piercing Shields on demand, it keeps all non-immune enemies from interfering with her for a short while, although it is a one-time use. Outside of that, luring away fast peons like [[Gabriel]] closer to the Cat Base can give 886-2 a decent head-start on her animations while the bigger threats play catchup.

What do you get for all of this tedium? Well, only the longest [[Freeze]] duration in the game, clocking in at a whopping 8 seconds vs. Aku and 9.6 seconds vs. Floating respectively (~47%/~56.4% uptime against Aku/Floating). The magnitude of this crowd-control is almost unheard of, especially for an ability as powerful as Freeze. To top things off, she has a 100% chance to [[Shield Piercing|Pierce Shields]] and [[Knockback]] target traits, distancing distance herself from the frontlines until she's ready to attack again. The possibilities for what you can do with an 8-second Freeze duration are nigh-endless, you can even file your taxes in that amount of time! Thus 886-2 pairs exceptionally well with rushers like [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] and [[Sanada Yukimura (Uber Rare Cat)|Immortal Yukimura]] to unload unfathomable amounts of damage at any given moment, sometimes completely unopposed. Her burst DPH isn't all too shabby either, dealing enough to instantly stagger enemies like [[Fallen Bear]] and [[Prof. Owlbrowley]] into fatal ranges of HP, if not outright killing them at a high enough level. Aku enemies are generally on the lesser-end of durability, as the majority of them have their effective HP centralized into their [[Shield]] like [[Le'Behemoth]], [[Midnite D.]], and the aforementioned Ackey. Being such a reliable Shield Piercer goes a long way into making her as good of an anti-Aku as she is. Floating is one of the bulkiest traits in the game, where almost every relevant threat has well over 1 million HP at standard [[Uncanny Legends]] magnification. The lot of them are hyper-aggressive, which means the moments of respite that 886-2 provides you from them is very valuable. Overall, if you protect her well enough, you'll be presented with many opportunities to press the advantage, making her a phenomenal clutch tool in the right moments.

[[Sage Slayer]] is realistically only useful against three enemies: Prof. Owlbrowley, [[Sage of Mind Soractes]], and [[Marquis Clionius]]. All three of them outrange 886-2, but as the story goes, they're usually all accompanied by short-ranged peons who she will have no trouble taking advantage of. Furthermore, Sage Slayer's 2x HP boost makes her a defensive monster at higher levels in tandem with Dodge, to the point where she can sometimes facetank direct confrontations with Sage of Mind Soractes without so much as flinching, given the right circumstances. Marquis Clionus is more questionable, since its DPH and effective range match her own. Clionius can almost deny her the opportunity to attack entirely if Dodge RNG isn't on your side, so be wary of that if you decide to use her against it. Her resistances are pretty good, with [[Surge Immunity]] being the most notable here in preventing gradual damage buildup from Aku Death Surges. [[Curse Immunity]] is practically a necessity to ensure her crowd-control doesn't get nullified by Floating Relics such as [[Lowkey]], meanwhile [[Toxic Immunity]] is pretty much just for [[Gobble]] and [[Zollow]]. [[Knockback Immunity]] facilitates usage against [[Poultrio]] (and [[Diabrollow]]), speaking volumes to her utility given the distinct lack of reliable non-[[Ultra Form]], non FEST counters to [[Invasion of Poultrio]]. All in all, 886-2 is a very good unit for those who know how to use her effectively, although she can be very finicky to work around in mixed stages.

